# Terms of the System Reference Document 5.1 (English, CC-BY-4.0, see the tab license), by hand;
# page numbers of SRD_CC_v5.1.pdf. Variant name: the term written out, where the term is an
# abbreviation; cover has the variants half, three-quarters and total. Names of the 2014 rules only.

# Damage types: p. 97 ("Damage Types"); the phrase as after the dice in stat blocks, e.g.
# p. 218 "7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) necrotic damage"
Rules/Damage/acid: acid
Rules/Damage/acid/Phrase: acid damage
Rules/Damage/bludgeoning: bludgeoning
Rules/Damage/bludgeoning/Phrase: bludgeoning damage
Rules/Damage/cold: cold
Rules/Damage/cold/Phrase: cold damage
Rules/Damage/fire: fire
Rules/Damage/fire/Phrase: fire damage
Rules/Damage/force: force
Rules/Damage/force/Phrase: force damage
Rules/Damage/lightning: lightning
Rules/Damage/lightning/Phrase: lightning damage
Rules/Damage/necrotic: necrotic
Rules/Damage/necrotic/Phrase: necrotic damage
Rules/Damage/piercing: piercing
Rules/Damage/piercing/Phrase: piercing damage
Rules/Damage/poison: poison
Rules/Damage/poison/Phrase: poison damage
Rules/Damage/psychic: psychic
Rules/Damage/psychic/Phrase: psychic damage
Rules/Damage/radiant: radiant
Rules/Damage/radiant/Phrase: radiant damage
Rules/Damage/slashing: slashing
Rules/Damage/slashing/Phrase: slashing damage
Rules/Damage/thunder: thunder
Rules/Damage/thunder/Phrase: thunder damage

# Abilities: stat block p. 218 "STR DEX CON INT WIS CHA"; names p. 76 ("Ability Scores and Modifiers");
# save: short for "<Ability> saving throw", e.g. p. 10 "a Wisdom saving throw"
Rules/Term/str: STR
Rules/Term/str/name: Strength
Rules/Term/str/save: STR save
Rules/Term/dex: DEX
Rules/Term/dex/name: Dexterity
Rules/Term/dex/save: DEX save
Rules/Term/con: CON
Rules/Term/con/name: Constitution
Rules/Term/con/save: CON save
Rules/Term/int: INT
Rules/Term/int/name: Intelligence
Rules/Term/int/save: INT save
Rules/Term/wis: WIS
Rules/Term/wis/name: Wisdom
Rules/Term/wis/save: WIS save
Rules/Term/cha: CHA
Rules/Term/cha/name: Charisma
Rules/Term/cha/save: CHA save

# Terms: AC p. 62 "Armor Class (AC)"; HP p. 116 table "Size HP AC" (= de p. 149);
# DC p. 77 "Difficulty Class ... DC"; CR p. 15 "Destroy Undead (CR 1/2)" (= de p. 30);
# XP p. 258 "experience points (XP)"; GM p. 12 "before the GM says" (= de p. 12), "the game master" p. 59.
# The SRD 5.1 says GM, not DM (182 times GM, never DM). Proficiency bonus: p. 8 class table
# "Level Proficiency Bonus" (91 times written out); the SRD 5.1 never abbreviates it, PB is the
# abbreviation in use (to be checked in the review of all terms).
Rules/Term/ac: AC
Rules/Term/ac/name: Armor Class
Rules/Term/hp: HP
Rules/Term/hp/name: hit points
Rules/Term/dc: DC
Rules/Term/dc/name: Difficulty Class
Rules/Term/cr: CR
Rules/Term/cr/name: challenge rating
Rules/Term/xp: XP
Rules/Term/xp/name: experience points
Rules/Term/gm: GM
Rules/Term/gm/name: game master
Rules/Term/pb: PB
Rules/Term/pb/name: proficiency bonus

# Conditions: p. 358-359 (Appendix PH-A); lowercase as in running text, e.g. p. 358 "a blinded
# creature", "the prone condition"
Rules/Term/blinded: blinded
Rules/Term/charmed: charmed
Rules/Term/deafened: deafened
Rules/Term/exhaustion: exhaustion
Rules/Term/frightened: frightened
Rules/Term/grappled: grappled
Rules/Term/incapacitated: incapacitated
Rules/Term/invisible: invisible
Rules/Term/paralyzed: paralyzed
Rules/Term/petrified: petrified
Rules/Term/poisoned: poisoned
Rules/Term/prone: prone
Rules/Term/restrained: restrained
Rules/Term/stunned: stunned
Rules/Term/unconscious: unconscious

# Actions: action p. 90 ("take one action"), bonus action p. 90 ("Bonus Actions"), reaction p. 91,
# opportunity attack p. 95; the actions in combat p. 93-94 ("Actions in Combat"), capitalized as in
# p. 93 "When you take the Dash action"
Rules/Term/action: action
Rules/Term/bonus-action: bonus action
Rules/Term/reaction: reaction
Rules/Term/opportunity-attack: opportunity attack
Rules/Term/attack: Attack
Rules/Term/cast-a-spell: Cast a Spell
Rules/Term/dash: Dash
Rules/Term/disengage: Disengage
Rules/Term/dodge: Dodge
Rules/Term/help: Help
Rules/Term/hide: Hide
Rules/Term/ready: Ready
Rules/Term/search: Search
Rules/Term/use-an-object: Use an Object

# Rolls, rest, damage and cover: inspiration p. 59; advantage and disadvantage p. 76; proficiency
# and ability check p. 77; saving throw p. 83; short and long rest p. 87 (p. 87 "spend one or more
# Hit Dice at the end of a short rest", Hit Dice always capitalized); initiative p. 90; attack roll
# p. 94; cover p. 96 (half, three-quarters and total cover), critical hit p. 96; resistance and
# vulnerability p. 97 ("Damage Resistance and Vulnerability"), immunity p. 257 ("Vulnerabilities,
# Resistances, and Immunities"); death saving throw and temporary hit points p. 98
Rules/Term/advantage: advantage
Rules/Term/disadvantage: disadvantage
Rules/Term/ability-check: ability check
Rules/Term/saving-throw: saving throw
Rules/Term/attack-roll: attack roll
Rules/Term/critical-hit: critical hit
Rules/Term/initiative: initiative
Rules/Term/inspiration: inspiration
Rules/Term/proficiency: proficiency
Rules/Term/death-saving-throw: death saving throw
Rules/Term/hit-dice: Hit Dice
Rules/Term/temporary-hit-points: temporary hit points
Rules/Term/short-rest: short rest
Rules/Term/long-rest: long rest
Rules/Term/resistance: resistance
Rules/Term/immunity: immunity
Rules/Term/vulnerability: vulnerability
Rules/Term/cover: cover
Rules/Term/cover/half: half cover
Rules/Term/cover/three-quarters: three-quarters cover
Rules/Term/cover/total: total cover

